originalClaim.observed:
The new family covers the activity bar, simulation controls, zoom pill and tab icons. The legacy painted family covers:
- the flesh-coloured hand of the Interact tool (240,184,160) with a black outline;
- the green/yellow image-tool picture;
- the wire tool with green and purple dots;
- the black-filled register 'pages' icon;
- palette I/O and Displays tiles: solid red LED, green/grey LED bar, RGB pie, red 7-seg, blue 'B' button, blue DIP, blue 'Hel' TTY, 'Local Bus', green PLA;
- white chip-with-magnifier icons in the Simulate tree;
- SoC 'uP' icons in Find Action.

Stroke weights, sizes (hand ≈ 28 px vs gates ≈ 20 px) and colour logic all differ. This is exactly the 'recognise the old software' problem.
